Undead creatures are immune to items of "Death". Zombies, mummies, 
skeletons, wraiths, vampires, liches... that type of creature. They're 
already dead.

basically, a Lich is an undead sorcerer. In classic D&D, a sorcerer who has 
performed magic to store his soul somewhere else so he can outlive the death 
or destruction of his body (and, sometimes even, create a new one or 
regenerate the old one to full health, when killed: the only way to 
permanently destroy him is to find and destroy the phylactery where he keeps 
his soul.) In Nethack, they don't bother with that much of an explanation, 
but he's still an UNDEAD sorcerer.

